{"title":"Conference Report and Intelligence Briefing: ACEID/ACP/AGen2025","link":"https://iafor.org/conference-report-and-intelligence-briefing-aceid-acp-agen-2025/","date":1748316204000,"content":"<img width=\"150\" height=\"150\" src=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-150x150.jpg\" alt=\"ACEID/ACP/AGen2025 Conference Report\" srcset=\"https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-150x150.jpg 150w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-600x600.jpg 600w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-100x100.jpg 100w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-50x50.jpg 50w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-300x300.jpg 300w, https://iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/ACEID2025-TDV02183-1500-32x32.jpg 32w\" />839 delegates from 62 countries participated in ACEID/ACP/AGen2025, representing 529 institutions and organisations worldwide. The conference offered an interdisciplinary lens between education, international development, psychology, and gerontology to discuss contemporary threats to humanity and human intelligence.\n<p><a href=\"https://iafor.org/conference-report-and-intelligence-briefing-aceid-acp-agen-2025/\">Source</a></p>","author":"IAFOR","siteTitle":"The International Academic Forum (IAFOR)","siteHash":"db6175d8277e1d8dd86d5cc607b1dd9335cce255aa7e00b46d0931f23a0d47f6","entryHash":"226d2ef082d73b03ecd2718b23d75a25090ece53a857dbf551d0b12f006405f4","category":"Interdisciplinary"}